From 9be5eb7bb104de95f2db19c97403fd37ed03897f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:08:23 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/34] toolkit: Places windows in the usable area, with a
 'Center' policy.

New windows were placed starting at the output's top-left (0, 0), below
the Clip, docks and other panels. Maximized windows also covered them:
The maximize extents were the output minus one tile size.

* Layers store the usable area of each output (extents minus the panels'
  exclusive zones), and wlmtk_desktop_get_usable_area() combines that
  across the desktop's layers.
* Maximize extents are the desktop's usable area, if the workspace has a
  desktop. This addresses the roadmap item for the dock's exclusive zone.
* Window placement uses the usable area of the output under the pointer,
  and the desktop's policy (wlmtk_desktop_set_window_placement()):
  'Center' centers the window, cascading if it would exactly cover
  another window -- as Window Maker's `WindowPlacement = center`. 'Smart'
  (default) is the earlier algorithm of filling free spots, now within
  the usable area.
* wlmtk_workspace_map_window_with_hint() permits a requested position
  (eg. by X11 clients) and a parent to center transients on.
* The window is kept within the usable area, at its top-left if larger,
  so that the title bar remains reachable. A window is placed only once:
  When mapped again (eg. on another workspace), it keeps its position.

Adds a unit test for center placement, hints and maximize extents.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
